Summary:
On the next day, the session focused on revising the concepts of React and its role in front-end development. We reviewed the fundamentals of React, including components, JSX, props, and state management. The session also covered how to structure a React application and reuse components effectively. Additionally, we revisited how React interacts with backend services to fetch and display data dynamically. This revision helped in strengthening the understanding of building interactive user interfaces.

Outcomes:
By the end of the session, we improved our understanding of core React concepts and component-based architecture. We gained more confidence in creating and managing reusable components within a React application. The revision also helped us understand how to integrate React with backend APIs for dynamic data handling. Overall, it prepared us to efficiently work on the front-end part of our projects. 
